inSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Updated the language on the error.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, yes the Shader Parameters are automatically created. A Texture2D Node (which could have an embedded texture) is converted to a Uniform in the GD Shader Code, which will be recognized as a Shader Parameter.\r\n\r\nThe VisualShader in the MRP has 2 Texture2D Nodes, they convert to code \r\n```\r\nuniform sampler2D tex_frg_44;\r\nuniform sampler2D tex_frg_43;\r\n```\r\nAnd when the converted GDShader is attached to a ShaderMaterial, the uniforms show up as a parameter again","created_at":"2025-09-16T23:36:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T23:36:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#discussion_r2353872157","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109375","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2353872157"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109375#discussion_r2353872157"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.githu